# Title: Potential PHP Reverse Shell
# ID: c6714a24-d7d5-4283-a36b-3ffd091d5f7e
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: @d4ns4n_
# Date: 2023-04-07
# Tags: attack.execution
# Description: Detects usage of the PHP CLI with the "-r" flag which allows it to run inline PHP code. The rule looks for calls to the "fsockopen" function which allows the creation of sockets.
# Attackers often leverage this in combination with functions such as "exec" or "fopen" to initiate a reverse shell connection.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(process.executable:*/php* AND (process.command_line:* -r * AND process.command_line:*fsockopen*) AND (process.command_line:*ash* OR process.command_line:*bash* OR process.command_line:*bsh* OR process.command_line:*csh* OR process.command_line:*ksh* OR process.command_line:*pdksh* OR process.command_line:*sh* OR process.command_line:*tcsh* OR process.command_line:*zsh*))
